1
00:00:06,923 --> 00:00:07,965
Jane.

2
00:00:10,092 --> 00:00:12,386
Jane? Care to join us?

3
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:14,722
The Moon's at perigee

4
00:00:15,139 --> 00:00:16,724
closest to the Earth.

5
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:19,435
- It's beautiful, isn't it?
- Yes, it is.

6
00:00:19,727 --> 00:00:22,396
- But the victim is over here.
- I know.

7
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:26,567
Work.

8
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,242
Victim's name's Eleanor Artega,
shot in the chest.

9
00:00:34,408 --> 00:00:35,993
There were reports
of gunshots around 11:00.

10
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,496
- Is she from the neighborhood?
- ID gives an address across town

11
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:41,040
but one of the Sac PD officers
said she grew up in the neighborhood.

12
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:42,792
Her mother runs a grocery
a few blocks away.

13
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:46,546
Pretty dress. Maybe she was coming
from some kind of event, wedding?

14
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:48,589
Performance, more like it.
She's a musician.

15
00:00:48,756 --> 00:00:50,967
- Some kind of stringed instrument.
- Because?

16
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:52,885
Because of the calluses
on her fingertips

17
00:00:53,052 --> 00:00:56,180
and the faint piney scent
of rosin on her dress.

18
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:58,307
Been a couple of gang
initiation killings in the area.

19
00:00:58,474 --> 00:01:00,560
Could be another one.
I'll talk to the Sac PD Gang Unit

20
00:01:00,726 --> 00:01:02,603
- see who's active.
- We'll canvass the looky-loos.

21
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,106
Hydrangea petal.

22
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:08,985
Interesting decoration
for a gang slaying

23
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:11,445
unless the crips have
taken up flower arranging

24
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:14,198
which I can definitely see
the therapeutic benefits of.

25
00:01:15,658 --> 00:01:17,535
- Thank you.
- Evidence, I believe.

26
00:01:19,745 --> 00:01:20,788
Come on.

27
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:27,086
And I'm looking for current information
on Norteño gangs in the northeast.

28
00:01:27,211 --> 00:01:28,796
Call me back as soon as possible.
Thanks.

29
00:01:30,089 --> 00:01:31,507
- Hey.
- Damn, man.

30
00:01:31,632 --> 00:01:32,675
You see I'm walking here, right?

31
00:01:33,259 --> 00:01:35,011
- You walked into me.
- Hell I did.

32
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:38,222
You need to get behind the line.
Police only here.

33
00:01:38,514 --> 00:01:41,225
- Trying to find out who killed that lady?
- You know somethin' about it?

34
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:43,185
Do I look like a snitch to you?

35
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:45,313
Keep walkin'.

36
00:01:46,772 --> 00:01:47,982
Go on.

37
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:53,070
Anything would be useful,
so if you wouldn't mind, just...

38
00:01:53,195 --> 00:01:56,032
Just give us a call and, uh,
thank you very much for your time.

39
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:58,909
I know it's slow,
but it's how the work is done.

40
00:01:59,035 --> 00:02:01,120
Yeah, I could point out someone
that knows something useful

41
00:02:01,245 --> 00:02:04,248
- with 25 words or less.
- Oh, really?

42
00:02:04,373 --> 00:02:05,416
Count 'em.

43
00:02:07,001 --> 00:02:08,044
Evening.

44
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:11,422
I have $100 for information
about the victim.

45
00:02:11,547 --> 00:02:12,840
$100.

46
00:02:17,261 --> 00:02:18,512
It's not $100.

47
00:02:18,804 --> 00:02:20,264
Just $1...

48
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:23,976
for information.

49
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:26,437
Any takers?

50
00:02:30,483 --> 00:02:31,734
25.

51
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:32,985
The point being...

52
00:02:33,152 --> 00:02:35,529
The gentleman in the plaid
shirt with the beanie

53
00:02:35,696 --> 00:02:36,947
didn't even consider raising his hand.

54
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:40,076
That means he has information
that not even $100 can buy.

55
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:41,661
Sir? Uh, you in the plaid

56
00:02:41,827 --> 00:02:43,454
we're gonna have to ask you
some questions.

57
00:02:44,288 --> 00:02:47,708
Cho, we got a runner! Get the car!
Head off around the block!

58
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,253
Someone took my keys.

59
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:54,924
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!
Stop the car!

60
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:56,634
Thanks for the ride, sucka!

61
00:03:00,721 --> 00:03:03,933
Come on, Starsky,
let's go get him. I'll drive.

62
00:03:04,642 --> 00:03:06,560
Stay over here!

63
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:13,609
Gonna walk home?

64
00:03:30,249 --> 00:03:32,459
Ms. Artega, we're very sorry
for your loss

65
00:03:32,584 --> 00:03:35,129
but we need to ask you some
questions about your daughter.

66
00:03:35,254 --> 00:03:36,505
I have work to do.

67
00:03:37,339 --> 00:03:39,591
Ma'am, what did Eleanor do
for a living?

68
00:03:39,717 --> 00:03:42,761
{\an8}She was a concert violinist
with the orchestra.

69
00:03:42,886 --> 00:03:46,306
{\an8}Dawn, I said the first shelf for these.

70
00:03:46,432 --> 00:03:47,808
Sorry, Ms. Artega.

71
00:03:49,893 --> 00:03:51,103
{\an8}First chair violin

72
00:03:52,396 --> 00:03:54,064
{\an8}the concertmaster

73
00:03:54,398 --> 00:03:57,151
{\an8}second to the conductor himself.

74
00:03:57,735 --> 00:03:59,987
{\an8}Youngest in symphony history.

75
00:04:00,654 --> 00:04:03,157
{\an8}- You must have been very proud.
- Proud, yes.

76
00:04:03,824 --> 00:04:06,285
{\an8}I was her manager.
We were a team.

77
00:04:08,454 --> 00:04:10,873
{\an8}Do you know why Eleanor was
in the neighborhood last night?

78
00:04:11,957 --> 00:04:13,542
{\an8}She came here.

79
00:04:13,751 --> 00:04:15,711
{\an8}She had given a solo performance

80
00:04:15,878 --> 00:04:18,005
{\an8}a special event. She wanted
to tell me about it.

81
00:04:20,048 --> 00:04:22,259
{\an8}Can you think of anyone
who may have wanted to harm her?

82
00:04:22,384 --> 00:04:23,552
{\an8}A boyfriend maybe?

83
00:04:23,844 --> 00:04:25,929
{\an8}She wasn't seeing anyone.
No time.

84
00:04:27,431 --> 00:04:28,766
{\an8}She used to have a boyfriend.

85
00:04:29,975 --> 00:04:31,226
Orlando Yglesias.

86
00:04:32,311 --> 00:04:33,353
Gangbanger.

87
00:04:33,896 --> 00:04:35,647
They dated about a year or so.

88
00:04:36,273 --> 00:04:37,316
Why would he wanna hurt her?

89
00:04:39,318 --> 00:04:41,612
{\an8}Eleanor broke it off six months ago.

90
00:04:41,779 --> 00:04:43,322
He wouldn't leave her alone.

91
00:04:43,655 --> 00:04:45,866
{\an8}He called, came to the apartment.

92
00:04:45,991 --> 00:04:47,284
{\an8}We had to get a restraining order!

93
00:04:49,203 --> 00:04:50,287
Dawn!

94
00:04:50,746 --> 00:04:51,997
Mop!

95
00:04:54,458 --> 00:04:56,168
How am I gonna clean this up?

96
00:04:57,002 --> 00:04:58,045
How am I gonna...

97
00:04:59,296 --> 00:05:00,547
Oh, my Ellie!

98
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:03,801
Oh, my baby.

99
00:05:06,261 --> 00:05:08,180
Why did they do this to you?

100
00:05:09,223 --> 00:05:10,808
Why?

101
00:05:17,105 --> 00:05:18,190
{\an8}"Hey, boss."

102
00:05:18,482 --> 00:05:20,025
{\an8}So I confirmed that Eleanor Artega

103
00:05:20,150 --> 00:05:21,777
{\an8}played a private event the night
that she was murdered.

104
00:05:21,902 --> 00:05:24,071
{\an8}Apparently celebrating
the, uh, recent purchase

105
00:05:24,196 --> 00:05:25,906
{\an8}by a collector of a, uh...
Wait for it...

106
00:05:26,031 --> 00:05:29,076
{\an8}"A Brescian Stradivarius violin."

107
00:05:29,201 --> 00:05:31,328
{\an8}I'm assuming that's a good one.
What about the boyfriend?

108
00:05:31,453 --> 00:05:34,289
{\an8}Orlando Yglesias, he's got a sheet,
some low-level stuff.

109
00:05:34,414 --> 00:05:36,375
{\an8}He runs with a Norteño gang
the, uh...

110
00:05:37,292 --> 00:05:39,086
{\an8}Lincoln Avenue Hermanos.

111
00:05:39,336 --> 00:05:41,046
Eleanor did have
a restraining order on him.

112
00:05:42,756 --> 00:05:44,758
This is the guy that fled
the scene last night

113
00:05:44,883 --> 00:05:46,635
the one that Jane picked out
from the crowd.

114
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:49,096
{\an8}Call Sac PD Gang Unit.
Tell them we need any help

115
00:05:49,263 --> 00:05:51,473
{\an8}- they can give finding this guy.
- Okay, you got it.

116
00:05:59,523 --> 00:06:00,566
{\an8}Jane?

117
00:06:01,984 --> 00:06:03,026
Jane.

118
00:06:04,987 --> 00:06:06,029
Jane.

119
00:06:08,782 --> 00:06:11,243
{\an8}We've got a little homicide
investigation going on here.

120
00:06:11,368 --> 00:06:12,411
{\an8}You care to join us?

121
00:06:12,536 --> 00:06:13,954
Yeah, I'm, I'm a little
busy right now.

122
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:16,999
{\an8}Brahms' Concerto in D Major.
Eleanor's the soloist.

123
00:06:17,124 --> 00:06:19,751
{\an8}She's very good,
very elegant, uh, rubato.

124
00:06:22,921 --> 00:06:25,382
Music later.
We have a viable suspect...

125
00:06:25,507 --> 00:06:26,675
The victim's ex-boyfriend.

126
00:06:26,842 --> 00:06:29,303
Meh. Wild goose chase, I hope.

127
00:06:29,469 --> 00:06:30,554
You hope? Why?

128
00:06:30,721 --> 00:06:32,973
Well, because if it is the boyfriend
then it's is boring

129
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:35,392
tragic, but dull

130
00:06:35,559 --> 00:06:37,394
which is to be avoided at all costs.

131
00:06:41,565 --> 00:06:42,733
Where you going?

132
00:06:45,777 --> 00:06:47,112
Jane?

133
00:06:53,535 --> 00:06:54,578
You Cho?

134
00:06:54,995 --> 00:06:57,331
- That's right.
- Beller, Sac PD.

135
00:06:57,456 --> 00:07:00,334
Anthony Rome. I picked him up
on Bellwood in the northwest.

136
00:07:00,459 --> 00:07:02,753
- Got your car, too. It's on its way.
- Thanks.

137
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,504
Juvenile Services is sending
someone to take him in?

138
00:07:04,671 --> 00:07:05,714
They're backed up.

139
00:07:05,839 --> 00:07:08,425
They can't process him
for 48 hours at the least.

140
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,011
Social worker says
his mother passed away.

141
00:07:11,136 --> 00:07:12,346
His father's in jail.

142
00:07:12,721 --> 00:07:15,057
She thinks we should release him
back to his foster family.

143
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:16,725
What gang put you up to this?

144
00:07:17,309 --> 00:07:18,644
I don't belong to a gang.

145
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:20,812
Stealing a cop car,
that's an initiation.

146
00:07:20,938 --> 00:07:22,397
You're jumping in with somebody.
Who?

147
00:07:23,065 --> 00:07:24,691
Beasty Mob? True Heights Villains?

148
00:07:24,816 --> 00:07:26,902
Sir, I don't know
what you're talking about.

149
00:07:27,194 --> 00:07:29,821
Hang on to him. Juvenile Services'll get
to him eventually.

150
00:07:29,947 --> 00:07:31,657
Yeah. No, I have a court
appearance today.

151
00:07:31,823 --> 00:07:33,367
I gotta unload him.
He's all yours.

152
00:07:33,742 --> 00:07:36,370
- I okayed it with your boss already.
- You're joking.

153
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:37,746
No joke.

154
00:07:38,664 --> 00:07:40,248
Thanks for your help, Officer Beller.

155
00:07:40,374 --> 00:07:42,250
- We appreciate the assist.
- No problem.

156
00:07:43,502 --> 00:07:46,380
- Boss...
- Sac PD are not babysitters.

157
00:07:46,505 --> 00:07:48,423
He stole your keys.
He's your problem.

158
00:07:48,715 --> 00:07:50,258
Make sure he doesn't take
anything else.

159
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,262
Sir, you gotta believe me
when I say how sorry I am.

160
00:07:54,388 --> 00:07:55,472
Don't talk.

161
00:07:55,597 --> 00:07:57,432
- No, really, I'm sorry.
- Not buying it.

162
00:07:58,016 --> 00:07:59,059
Come on.

163
00:07:59,518 --> 00:08:01,937
- Whatever, punk.
- That's more like it.

164
00:08:12,114 --> 00:08:13,156
Mr. Jane?

165
00:08:13,281 --> 00:08:15,742
Hi. I'm Kieran Carruthers
the company's outreach assistant.

166
00:08:16,243 --> 00:08:17,703
Front office said I might find you here.

167
00:08:17,953 --> 00:08:19,663
You're no bureaucrat.
You're a musician.

168
00:08:20,288 --> 00:08:21,957
Yes, I'm the principal oboist.

169
00:08:22,374 --> 00:08:24,042
Definitely oboesque.

170
00:08:25,752 --> 00:08:28,380
Concertmaster sits, uh, here, yes?

171
00:08:28,547 --> 00:08:29,589
Yes.

172
00:08:33,301 --> 00:08:34,594
Interesting bookmark.

173
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,972
- Yeah, looks like an expensive one.
- Really?

174
00:08:39,224 --> 00:08:40,267
Yeah.

175
00:08:41,685 --> 00:08:43,770
You know, if you tell me what you're
looking for, I might be able to help.

176
00:08:44,021 --> 00:08:45,313
I'm looking for a killer.

177
00:08:47,899 --> 00:08:49,985
I'm sorry.
Eleanor's killer? Here?

178
00:08:50,110 --> 00:08:52,487
You're musicians,
professional obsessives.

179
00:08:52,612 --> 00:08:54,364
Most kids spend
their teen years having fun.

180
00:08:54,531 --> 00:08:55,741
You spent them practicing scales.

181
00:08:55,866 --> 00:08:58,910
It's a noble pursuit but as a result,
you're all a little nutty.

182
00:08:59,036 --> 00:09:00,912
Well, uh, okay,
I don't know if I'd say that.

183
00:09:01,371 --> 00:09:02,998
There's a definite air
of unrest in the room.

184
00:09:03,123 --> 00:09:04,875
- What is that about?
- Right.

185
00:09:05,042 --> 00:09:07,335
We're supposed to start our season
a day after tomorrow.

186
00:09:07,461 --> 00:09:10,130
Opening night, big fund-raising
meet and greet with our donors.

187
00:09:10,297 --> 00:09:13,550
Some of us thought we should
postpone because of Eleanor

188
00:09:13,717 --> 00:09:15,761
but the, uh, maestro didn't agree.

189
00:09:16,303 --> 00:09:18,013
Your conductor...
A tyrant?

190
00:09:18,430 --> 00:09:21,808
Vincent Manheiser.
I wouldn't say he's a tyrant. He's just...

191
00:09:22,559 --> 00:09:23,769
not nice.

192
00:09:23,977 --> 00:09:25,687
All right, let's get to work.

193
00:09:25,854 --> 00:09:26,897
See for yourself.

194
00:09:27,064 --> 00:09:28,732
Come on, people. Let's go.

195
00:09:29,316 --> 00:09:32,152
Haven't got all day.
Up, up, up. Come on.

196
00:09:32,694 --> 00:09:33,737
All right.

197
00:09:36,615 --> 00:09:38,617
- Constance.
- Yes, maestro?

198
00:09:38,867 --> 00:09:41,286
You will take Eleanor's seat
as concertmaster.

199
00:09:43,038 --> 00:09:45,040
You've not shown any of her
natural gifts of leadership

200
00:09:45,207 --> 00:09:49,169
but under the circumstances,
we shall have to make do, yes?

201
00:09:50,587 --> 00:09:52,839
- I'll do my best.
- Ariel.

202
00:09:54,466 --> 00:09:57,427
Your keen lust for advancement
will be gratified.

203
00:09:57,844 --> 00:10:00,388
- Second seat for you.
- Yes, maestro.

204
00:10:02,349 --> 00:10:04,142
All right, everyone.
Ready?

205
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,020
From the top.

206
00:10:07,145 --> 00:10:08,188
And...

207
00:10:10,190 --> 00:10:11,566
And tension.

208
00:10:12,317 --> 00:10:13,443
Forte.

209
00:10:20,992 --> 00:10:22,911
Yep. Orlando Yglesias.

210
00:10:23,286 --> 00:10:24,663
Okay. Thanks.

211
00:10:25,747 --> 00:10:26,915
Gang Unit's gonna ask around

212
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:28,583
check out where the victim's
ex-boyfriend hangs.

213
00:10:28,708 --> 00:10:29,751
Good.

214
00:10:36,675 --> 00:10:37,717
There you go.

215
00:10:39,136 --> 00:10:40,262
I can't eat this.

216
00:10:41,179 --> 00:10:43,640
- Why not?
- I'm a vegetarian.

217
00:10:52,190 --> 00:10:53,233
Now it's vegetarian.

218
00:10:59,239 --> 00:11:01,366
Hey. Pick that up.

219
00:11:01,491 --> 00:11:02,868
You better not mess with Cho, man.

220
00:11:02,993 --> 00:11:04,494
He used to be an Avon Park Playboy.

221
00:11:04,661 --> 00:11:06,621
- You were a playboy?
- Oh, yeah. That's right.

222
00:11:07,914 --> 00:11:10,208
Then you should know my dad...
Lawrence Rome.

223
00:11:10,584 --> 00:11:12,252
Runs with the South Side Mafia.

224
00:11:12,836 --> 00:11:14,880
- Never heard of him. I'll be right back.
- All right.

225
00:11:19,509 --> 00:11:21,052
Wayne, I'm getting coffee.
Want some?

226
00:11:21,303 --> 00:11:22,470
Uh, no, thanks.

227
00:11:37,819 --> 00:11:38,862
Hey.

228
00:12:18,985 --> 00:12:20,070
Hey.

229
00:12:20,570 --> 00:12:22,072
- What is this?
- What?

230
00:12:22,197 --> 00:12:24,032
"I want you, baby. Come to me"?

231
00:12:24,699 --> 00:12:26,743
- Is this some kind of a joke?
- I didn't send that.

232
00:12:26,868 --> 00:12:29,079
- Well, it's on your phone.
- Well, my phone is on my desk.

233
00:12:30,288 --> 00:12:31,331
Hey.

234
00:12:31,831 --> 00:12:33,041
Who's watching the kid?

235
00:12:37,462 --> 00:12:38,505
Hey!

236
00:12:43,468 --> 00:12:44,594
Nice try.

237
00:12:47,764 --> 00:12:48,890
Let's go.

238
00:12:50,684 --> 00:12:52,394
- I had him.
- Yeah.

239
00:12:57,274 --> 00:13:00,068
- You can't do this. I'm a minor.
- Too bad.

240
00:13:02,362 --> 00:13:04,114
I know I shouldn't have messed
with you.

241
00:13:04,572 --> 00:13:05,699
I can't be here.

242
00:13:06,157 --> 00:13:08,034
I gotta go, for real.

243
00:13:08,785 --> 00:13:10,245
Gang Unit just called back.

244
00:13:10,370 --> 00:13:12,289
They say Orlando's crew hangs
at 8th and Market.

245
00:13:12,497 --> 00:13:13,623
We should go sit on it.

246
00:13:14,165 --> 00:13:16,209
You're looking
for Orlando Yglesias, right?

247
00:13:16,835 --> 00:13:19,296
I know him.
He's from the neighborhood.

248
00:13:19,504 --> 00:13:21,172
You ain't gonna find him
at 8th and Market.

249
00:13:21,339 --> 00:13:22,382
Why not?

250
00:13:22,507 --> 00:13:23,925
'Cause that's where
the Hermanos hang.

251
00:13:24,175 --> 00:13:25,593
Orlando's not with them no more.

252
00:13:26,094 --> 00:13:28,555
- Gang Unit says different.
- They don't know.

253
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:30,390
Jumped into a new gang
a couple months ago.

254
00:13:30,515 --> 00:13:31,683
Yeah? Which one?

255
00:13:32,559 --> 00:13:34,394
Cut me loose, and I'll tell you.

256
00:13:37,272 --> 00:13:38,815
The Loco Pimps.

257
00:13:39,566 --> 00:13:42,652
House on Lex and Tremont,
that's their spot.

258
00:13:42,777 --> 00:13:44,821
Gang Unit says the information's
six months old.

259
00:13:45,405 --> 00:13:46,698
Kid could be right.

260
00:13:47,532 --> 00:13:50,118
Wouldn't hurt to check it out.
Lex and Tremont's close.

261
00:13:50,243 --> 00:13:52,746
If Orlando doesn't show up
we'll swing by the other location.

262
00:13:52,871 --> 00:13:55,040
If you get him, you'll let
me out, right?

263
00:13:56,249 --> 00:13:57,292
Let's go.

264
00:14:09,721 --> 00:14:11,431
You're dragging, people!

265
00:14:14,559 --> 00:14:15,977
Stay in tempo!

266
00:14:17,729 --> 00:14:18,772
Off the string.

267
00:14:20,190 --> 00:14:21,316
Off the string.

268
00:14:22,275 --> 00:14:24,486
Stop!
Stop. Stop.

269
00:14:25,528 --> 00:14:26,571
Ariel.

270
00:14:27,572 --> 00:14:30,450
B-flat? It's ridiculous, even for you.

271
00:14:31,159 --> 00:14:33,453
While we're on the subject,
Ann, Carol, you're dragging.

272
00:14:34,788 --> 00:14:36,373
Trumpets, measure 37...

273
00:14:36,498 --> 00:14:37,540
Soggy.

274
00:14:38,541 --> 00:14:41,127
I thought it sounded
perfectly lovely. Bravo.

275
00:14:41,753 --> 00:14:44,047
- You're awfully picky, aren't you?
- Who are you?

276
00:14:44,464 --> 00:14:47,217
Never mind. Go. Leave. Now.

277
00:14:47,342 --> 00:14:50,178
I'm with the CBI.
I'm here about the murder.

278
00:14:50,595 --> 00:14:52,764
Uh, if you'll please wait outside...

279
00:14:52,889 --> 00:14:55,725
- You hate being interrupted, don't you?
- As a matter of fact, I do.

280
00:14:56,101 --> 00:14:58,895
Interesting. I have one question,
then I'll leave.

281
00:14:59,396 --> 00:15:01,439
I know it was you that murdered
Eleanor Artega.

282
00:15:01,564 --> 00:15:03,274
I just need to know why, Vincent.

283
00:15:04,109 --> 00:15:05,318
Why did you kill her?

284
00:15:08,196 --> 00:15:09,280
You are crazy.

285
00:15:11,574 --> 00:15:14,953
That is exactly, exactly what
I thought you would say

286
00:15:15,370 --> 00:15:16,704
now I know for sure.

287
00:15:18,206 --> 00:15:19,332
Yes.

288
00:15:19,791 --> 00:15:21,084
You, sir

289
00:15:21,251 --> 00:15:23,753
are a cold-blooded murderer...

290
00:15:25,046 --> 00:15:26,840
And you will get what you deserve.

291
00:15:26,965 --> 00:15:29,801
I did not kill Eleanor Artega.

292
00:15:29,926 --> 00:15:32,512
- Are you sure of that?
- Very sure.

293
00:15:33,513 --> 00:15:36,141
- Meh. Well, it's worth a try.
- Worth a try?

294
00:15:36,266 --> 00:15:38,017
Yeah, the old "It was you" gambit.

295
00:15:38,601 --> 00:15:40,937
Guilty people often fold up
at that point...

296
00:15:41,062 --> 00:15:42,981
Guilty people with
a conscience, that is

297
00:15:43,106 --> 00:15:45,108
which means you're either innocent

298
00:15:45,567 --> 00:15:47,819
or you're a cold, heartless monster.

299
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,655
Or both.

300
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:52,282
This is an outrageous
abuse of authority.

301
00:15:52,407 --> 00:15:55,034
Yes, yes, I know. Don't go getting
on your high horse.

302
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:57,162
It still might be you, and if it is...

303
00:16:00,832 --> 00:16:02,542
justice will find you.

304
00:16:24,353 --> 00:16:25,396
What?

305
00:16:25,521 --> 00:16:26,731
We're wasting our time.

306
00:16:27,315 --> 00:16:29,108
Orlando's not gonna show up.
The kid played us.

307
00:16:29,233 --> 00:16:30,985
Sounded like he knew
what he was talking about.

308
00:16:31,110 --> 00:16:32,403
He knows how to sell it.

309
00:16:32,737 --> 00:16:34,447
Ah, he doesn't seem that bad to me.

310
00:16:35,072 --> 00:16:36,657
I used to be that kid.

311
00:16:37,116 --> 00:16:39,243
Any chance to mess
with a cop, I'd do it.

312
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:40,786
Hey, check it out.

313
00:16:50,755 --> 00:16:53,090
- That's Orlando, isn't it?
- Yeah. Go. Go.

314
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:01,766
CBI.

315
00:17:01,891 --> 00:17:03,392
Let me see your hands. Do it.

316
00:17:08,105 --> 00:17:09,607
Tell me about Eleanor.

317
00:17:17,198 --> 00:17:19,575
Orlando, you wanna talk
after spending the night

318
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:21,619
in a holding cell, that's your right

319
00:17:22,203 --> 00:17:23,412
but tomorrow morning

320
00:17:23,538 --> 00:17:26,290
I am still gonna be asking you
the same questions.

321
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:28,543
What you wanna know?

322
00:17:29,585 --> 00:17:31,462
You were an unlikely couple.

323
00:17:31,587 --> 00:17:33,756
Eleanor was in the orchestra.
She was moving her way up.

324
00:17:33,881 --> 00:17:36,509
You weren't.
Then she dumps you.

325
00:17:36,634 --> 00:17:38,052
Must have been stressful.

326
00:17:38,803 --> 00:17:40,638
- Did it make you angry?
- Yeah, here we go.

327
00:17:40,763 --> 00:17:43,307
- Jamming me up for this.
- I'm just askin'.

328
00:17:43,766 --> 00:17:45,393
I wasn't angry.

329
00:17:46,143 --> 00:17:48,396
Eleanor was all about music, always.

330
00:17:49,021 --> 00:17:51,357
Wasn't gonna let me or anyone else
get in the way of that.

331
00:17:51,941 --> 00:17:54,610
- I respected that.
- Then why'd you keep calling?

332
00:17:54,735 --> 00:17:56,279
Going over to her apartment?

333
00:17:57,697 --> 00:18:00,700
We were cool.
There was no reason not to hang.

334
00:18:00,866 --> 00:18:02,702
Except a restraining order.

335
00:18:02,952 --> 00:18:05,246
Her mother made her do that.
She told me.

336
00:18:05,371 --> 00:18:08,082
Her mom thought I was moving in again
'cause I came by a couple times.

337
00:18:08,207 --> 00:18:11,502
If you're such a stand-up guy
why did you run from the crime scene?

338
00:18:11,627 --> 00:18:13,254
A cop calls me out, what I'm gonna do?

339
00:18:16,299 --> 00:18:18,009
I wouldn't hurt El.

340
00:18:18,384 --> 00:18:19,969
Didn't want nothin' but good for her.

341
00:18:21,679 --> 00:18:23,264
Believe it, don't...

342
00:18:23,514 --> 00:18:24,807
I don't control you.

343
00:18:26,976 --> 00:18:30,104
I talked to the clerk of the judge
who issued the restraining order.

344
00:18:30,438 --> 00:18:31,564
Orlando's right.

345
00:18:31,689 --> 00:18:34,317
Eleanor did ask for it
but her mother was the driving force.

346
00:18:34,442 --> 00:18:35,568
That's not what Isabella said.

347
00:18:35,693 --> 00:18:37,570
Also, I checked Eleanor's e-mails.

348
00:18:37,695 --> 00:18:39,530
Eleanor fired Isabella as her manager

349
00:18:39,655 --> 00:18:41,115
and hired a new one
just a couple weeks ago.

350
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:43,075
I bet that didn't go over well
with the mom.

351
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:46,287
New manager says Eleanor
and her mother weren't speaking.

352
00:18:46,454 --> 00:18:49,457
They spoke before she died.
Go talk to Isabella again.

353
00:18:49,582 --> 00:18:51,417
- Find out what they really said.
- Okay, I'm on it.

354
00:18:55,588 --> 00:18:56,672
You'll sleep here.

355
00:18:58,257 --> 00:18:59,800
The door will be locked
but there's someone down the hall.

356
00:18:59,925 --> 00:19:01,552
You need anything,
just bang on the door, okay?

357
00:19:02,261 --> 00:19:03,721
But I'm leaving tomorrow, right?

358
00:19:03,846 --> 00:19:05,473
Depends on when Juvenile Services
gets here.

359
00:19:05,765 --> 00:19:07,141
Juvenile Services?

360
00:19:07,266 --> 00:19:09,268
You said you'd let me go
if I gave you Orlando.

361
00:19:09,518 --> 00:19:11,437
- We had a deal.
- There was no deal.

362
00:19:11,604 --> 00:19:13,397
Come on, man.
Don't punk out on me.

363
00:19:14,231 --> 00:19:15,858
I'm not kidding.
I need to get out of here.

364
00:19:15,983 --> 00:19:17,568
Well, you should've thought of that
before you stole a car.

365
00:19:17,693 --> 00:19:19,862
- No, I've got business.
- It'll have to wait.

366
00:19:21,030 --> 00:19:22,448
- Hey.
- Let me go!

367
00:19:22,740 --> 00:19:24,241
Get off me!

368
00:19:24,367 --> 00:19:26,535
Get off of me, man!
Let me go!

369
00:19:26,786 --> 00:19:29,705
- Hey. Stop. Stop.
- Get off of me, man!

370
00:19:29,830 --> 00:19:31,874
- Easy.
- Get off of me!

371
00:19:38,714 --> 00:19:40,883
Look at me. Look at me.

372
00:19:44,303 --> 00:19:45,638
What's this really about?

373
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:51,018
I'm not leaving until you tell me.

374
00:19:51,811 --> 00:19:53,604
My dad got arrested.

375
00:19:54,730 --> 00:19:56,440
They say he robbed a liquor store

376
00:19:57,149 --> 00:19:58,317
but he didn't.

377
00:20:01,028 --> 00:20:02,071
All right.

378
00:20:02,488 --> 00:20:03,531
He didn't.

379
00:20:04,532 --> 00:20:06,200
He's got an alibi.

380
00:20:06,826 --> 00:20:08,661
Dude named Jayden Stephens.

381
00:20:09,704 --> 00:20:11,205
But Jayden won't come forward.

382
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:13,708
He's got warrants
out on him, so he's hiding.

383
00:20:14,667 --> 00:20:16,544
But my dad's going on trial next week.

384
00:20:18,504 --> 00:20:20,089
I can't find Jayden.

385
00:20:20,881 --> 00:20:22,508
My dad's going to prison.

386
00:20:25,511 --> 00:20:27,054
That's why I stole your car.

387
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:29,849
Jayden's running
with the True Heights Villains.

388
00:20:30,641 --> 00:20:33,060
I was thinking
if I can jump in with them

389
00:20:34,186 --> 00:20:35,855
they'd tell me where he's hiding.

390
00:20:37,106 --> 00:20:38,566
Figured they'd know.

391
00:20:42,737 --> 00:20:44,864
You were joining a gang
to get your father outta prison.

392
00:20:46,282 --> 00:20:47,533
Yeah.

393
00:20:51,162 --> 00:20:52,538
Try to get some sleep.

394
00:21:09,930 --> 00:21:11,640
We know Eleanor fired you
as her manager.

395
00:21:11,766 --> 00:21:14,935
- Why didn't you tell us that?
- I didn't think it was important.

396
00:21:15,060 --> 00:21:16,228
Well, you must've talked about it

397
00:21:16,353 --> 00:21:18,189
the night Eleanor came here
and she was killed.

398
00:21:20,149 --> 00:21:21,317
We did.

399
00:21:22,651 --> 00:21:24,612
She wanted to make up. I didn't.

400
00:21:25,905 --> 00:21:27,406
I should've, but I didn't.

401
00:21:27,907 --> 00:21:30,201
So the last time you spoke, you fought?

402
00:21:32,953 --> 00:21:35,790
Are you asking if I killed
my daughter?

403
00:21:36,207 --> 00:21:38,042
No, ma'am, I'm just trying
to get the facts straight.

404
00:21:38,167 --> 00:21:39,376
Yes, she is.

405
00:21:42,463 --> 00:21:43,714
I mean, come on, you are.

406
00:21:47,051 --> 00:21:49,470
Most kids never make it out
of this neighborhood.

407
00:21:50,346 --> 00:21:51,847
Eleanor did

408
00:21:52,598 --> 00:21:55,851
because I gave her everything
so she could have a better life.

409
00:21:57,144 --> 00:21:59,939
- Why would I hurt her?
- Grace, it's clear as day.

410
00:22:00,064 --> 00:22:01,982
Isabella had nothing to do
with her daughter's death.

411
00:22:02,107 --> 00:22:04,568
More importantly,
was Eleanor into cats?

412
00:22:05,778 --> 00:22:07,530
Cats? No.

413
00:22:07,655 --> 00:22:10,950
What about ancient Egypt, pyramids?
Mummies?

414
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:14,787
No. She never talked to me
about Egypt.

415
00:22:15,746 --> 00:22:18,290
Okay.
Thanks. Let's roll.

416
00:22:20,167 --> 00:22:22,545
"And I look forward to seeing all of you
tomorrow night"

417
00:22:22,670 --> 00:22:24,922
"as our 73rd season begins."

418
00:22:25,381 --> 00:22:28,300
So to all our donors, our board members

419
00:22:28,425 --> 00:22:30,302
our most loyal supporters

420
00:22:30,469 --> 00:22:32,471
I say thank you.

421
00:22:43,023 --> 00:22:46,110
Is that for Ariel?
More of a red wine girl, I would think.

422
00:22:46,777 --> 00:22:47,903
How'd you know this was for her?

423
00:22:48,028 --> 00:22:50,364
Well, clearly,
you've got a thing for her.

424
00:22:50,739 --> 00:22:53,284
Word to the wise,
she likes the bad boys.

425
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,329
- Oh, you're back.
- Mm.

426
00:22:57,454 --> 00:22:59,790
- Don't let Vincent see you.
- I think I can take him.

427
00:22:59,915 --> 00:23:02,126
Oh, can I watch?
That was fun last time.

428
00:23:02,251 --> 00:23:05,671
This is not a joke, Ariel.
I'm following up on an important clue.

429
00:23:05,796 --> 00:23:07,673
It could very well break the case.

430
00:23:10,801 --> 00:23:11,969
Well, come on.

431
00:23:14,013 --> 00:23:15,306
You're gonna tell us, right?

432
00:23:16,891 --> 00:23:19,685
- He can't, Ariel.
- Oh, we won't say anything.

433
00:23:20,102 --> 00:23:21,896
- Promise.
- I'd like to know.

434
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:25,566
Well, I suppose
you're gonna hear soon enough.

435
00:23:29,570 --> 00:23:33,032
Eleanor was in a relationship
with someone from the orchestra.

436
00:23:34,408 --> 00:23:35,993
I suspected as much.

437
00:23:36,118 --> 00:23:37,494
Who was it?

438
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:40,539
- Uh, I can't...
- It couldn't be Douglas, could it?

439
00:23:41,457 --> 00:23:43,042
Or Howard?

440
00:23:43,292 --> 00:23:44,960
Think bigger. That's all I'm saying.

441
00:23:48,964 --> 00:23:50,424
It wasn't...

442
00:23:52,843 --> 00:23:54,386
- No.
- Are you serious?

443
00:23:54,511 --> 00:23:55,804
Deadly.

444
00:23:58,182 --> 00:24:00,142
And he was abusing her...

445
00:24:00,768 --> 00:24:02,269
sexually.

446
00:24:02,478 --> 00:24:04,605
- That's awful.
- Yes.

447
00:24:07,149 --> 00:24:09,151
- Oh, my...
- I don't see it.

448
00:24:22,206 --> 00:24:23,457
ID please.

449
00:24:23,916 --> 00:24:26,001
"Mr. Rome, I'm Kimball Cho
with the CBI."

450
00:24:26,752 --> 00:24:28,337
Your son Anthony tells me
you're innocent

451
00:24:28,462 --> 00:24:30,089
of the charge you're facing.
Is that true?

452
00:24:30,339 --> 00:24:32,216
- Anthony told you that?
- Yeah.

453
00:24:32,341 --> 00:24:33,592
How you know my son?

454
00:24:33,759 --> 00:24:35,260
That's not important right now.

455
00:24:35,594 --> 00:24:37,763
Why the hell do you care
about any of this?

456
00:24:37,888 --> 00:24:39,306
I'm giving you a chance to say
you didn't do the crime.

457
00:24:39,431 --> 00:24:41,892
- You're not gonna take it?
- No. No, I didn't do it.

458
00:24:42,017 --> 00:24:43,060
DA says you did.

459
00:24:43,185 --> 00:24:45,312
Yeah, a store owner
picked me out of a lineup.

460
00:24:45,437 --> 00:24:46,814
Bad witness ID that's all.

461
00:24:46,981 --> 00:24:48,649
But you know how hard
that is to beat, right?

462
00:24:48,774 --> 00:24:50,317
And you've robbed
a lotta stores, haven't you?

463
00:24:51,402 --> 00:24:54,238
- Not anymore. That is all behind me.
- Since when?

464
00:24:56,448 --> 00:24:59,201
Since Anthony's mother
passed about a year ago.

465
00:24:59,326 --> 00:25:01,286
I've been trying to step up, do better.

466
00:25:01,453 --> 00:25:03,455
Look, I even got a new construction job.

467
00:25:03,789 --> 00:25:05,582
And you run with the South Side Mafia.

468
00:25:07,126 --> 00:25:08,836
How do they feel about you
steppin' up?

469
00:25:10,170 --> 00:25:12,715
I'm jumping out as soon as
I put all this behind me.

470
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,633
You've had a year to jump out.
What are you waiting for?

471
00:25:14,967 --> 00:25:17,720
Man, the hell with you!
You don't know me!

472
00:25:19,763 --> 00:25:21,265
DA offered you two years.

473
00:25:21,598 --> 00:25:23,517
You could do that much time easily.

474
00:25:23,642 --> 00:25:24,935
Why'd you turn it down?

475
00:25:25,060 --> 00:25:27,855
Two years of my boy in foster care
out there on the streets?

476
00:25:27,980 --> 00:25:29,940
He would be dead or in a cell
with me.

477
00:25:30,232 --> 00:25:32,651
No. I been gone too long.

478
00:25:33,110 --> 00:25:34,695
I have got to get outta here.

479
00:25:39,616 --> 00:25:40,993
Tell me about Jayden Stephens.

480
00:25:47,833 --> 00:25:49,043
I got your message.

481
00:25:49,168 --> 00:25:51,754
- Just in time. The fun will soon begin.
- What's going on?

482
00:25:52,504 --> 00:25:54,089
It's just horrible, isn't it?

483
00:25:54,757 --> 00:25:57,301
- What is, ma'am?
- Our conductor...

484
00:25:58,594 --> 00:26:02,598
has been having an illicit relationship
with our poor, dear Eleanor.

485
00:26:02,848 --> 00:26:03,891
No.

486
00:26:04,016 --> 00:26:05,100
Yes.

487
00:26:05,350 --> 00:26:07,478
And he hit her.

488
00:26:09,354 --> 00:26:12,232
- Allison! Excuse me.
- You're excused.

489
00:26:14,234 --> 00:26:16,070
You. Why?

490
00:26:16,403 --> 00:26:17,613
Lure out the real lover.

491
00:26:19,281 --> 00:26:20,365
Oops. Gotta go.

492
00:26:25,746 --> 00:26:27,706
Someone in the orchestra had
a passionate

493
00:26:27,831 --> 00:26:29,374
and unrequited crush on Eleanor.

494
00:26:29,500 --> 00:26:30,667
And you know this because?

495
00:26:30,793 --> 00:26:33,420
Cats and Egypt...
Eleanor wasn't into them.

496
00:26:33,629 --> 00:26:35,172
The bookmark, she didn't buy it
for herself

497
00:26:35,297 --> 00:26:37,174
and it's too expensive
for a casual gift.

498
00:26:37,299 --> 00:26:40,219
Someone was trying very hard
to impress her.

499
00:26:40,552 --> 00:26:41,929
Now thanks to the rumor mill

500
00:26:42,054 --> 00:26:44,515
that person thinks that Vincent
was sleeping with Eleanor.

501
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:46,141
Add in a couple of glasses
of champagne

502
00:26:46,266 --> 00:26:48,894
- and if I haven't missed the mark...
- "You son of a bitch!"

503
00:26:49,144 --> 00:26:50,729
How could you do that to Eleanor?

504
00:26:50,854 --> 00:26:52,356
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

505
00:26:52,481 --> 00:26:53,774
- Don't lie to me.
- Here we go.

506
00:26:53,899 --> 00:26:55,025
Go home and sober up.

507
00:26:59,113 --> 00:27:01,323
That's enough!
Get off of him! Come on!

508
00:27:01,448 --> 00:27:04,451
Now. Break it up!
Break it up now!

509
00:27:04,827 --> 00:27:06,286
Break it up.

510
00:27:08,664 --> 00:27:11,250
Break it up!
Enough! Enough!

511
00:27:11,375 --> 00:27:13,127
Let me know if you need me
to call for backup.

512
00:27:14,753 --> 00:27:16,839
Oh! Hey!
I said, get your hands off!

513
00:27:24,361 --> 00:27:27,697
Constance, we know you bought
Eleanor that bookmark.

514
00:27:28,156 --> 00:27:30,408
We found the charge
on your credit card records.

515
00:27:31,618 --> 00:27:33,245
You were in love with her, weren't you?

516
00:27:34,537 --> 00:27:37,082
Yes, I was.

517
00:27:37,540 --> 00:27:38,750
When did you tell her?

518
00:27:40,877 --> 00:27:42,420
A few weeks ago.

519
00:27:43,338 --> 00:27:46,549
She was really, really nice, but...

520
00:27:48,218 --> 00:27:49,552
she wasn't interested.

521
00:27:49,886 --> 00:27:51,346
Did that upset you?

522
00:27:52,764 --> 00:27:54,307
I suppose a little.

523
00:27:55,392 --> 00:27:57,060
You have a temper, don't you?

524
00:27:58,019 --> 00:28:00,021
No. Hardly at all.

525
00:28:00,146 --> 00:28:01,856
Oh, you got pretty angry at Vincent.

526
00:28:02,565 --> 00:28:04,317
That was different.

527
00:28:04,442 --> 00:28:05,902
I, I thought...

528
00:28:06,111 --> 00:28:08,697
I heard Vincent hurt Eleanor.
I...

529
00:28:09,531 --> 00:28:11,324
I didn't think that was right.

530
00:28:11,449 --> 00:28:13,451
And what about the night
Eleanor died?

531
00:28:14,077 --> 00:28:15,578
Did you have a temper then?

532
00:28:17,372 --> 00:28:18,999
You knew she was playing that night.

533
00:28:19,124 --> 00:28:20,500
It wouldn't have been
that hard to follow her.

534
00:28:20,625 --> 00:28:22,085
You can't be serious.

535
00:28:23,003 --> 00:28:25,547
I don't think the fact that Vincent
had abused Eleanor

536
00:28:25,672 --> 00:28:27,132
is what upset you.

537
00:28:27,716 --> 00:28:30,218
I think you couldn't stand her
being with somebody else.

538
00:28:30,343 --> 00:28:31,636
No.

539
00:28:31,761 --> 00:28:33,263
All right, then explain this
for me then.

540
00:28:40,770 --> 00:28:43,481
Why was the gun that killed
Eleanor in your car?

541
00:28:44,274 --> 00:28:45,525
What?

542
00:28:45,650 --> 00:28:48,361
A few hours ago,
we found it in your trunk.

543
00:28:50,447 --> 00:28:52,073
That isn't mine.

544
00:28:52,240 --> 00:28:53,283
It's...

545
00:28:53,408 --> 00:28:55,577
Th, that's not mine. It isn't.

546
00:28:55,702 --> 00:28:58,330
That's not really an explanation
of how it got there.

547
00:28:59,748 --> 00:29:00,874
I...

548
00:29:01,416 --> 00:29:03,168
I,I want a lawyer.

549
00:29:04,169 --> 00:29:05,211
Please.

550
00:29:19,684 --> 00:29:21,311
So, Constance.

551
00:29:22,145 --> 00:29:23,313
We're charging her.

552
00:29:23,855 --> 00:29:25,482
Then we can all rest easy.

553
00:29:29,444 --> 00:29:30,612
Say it.

554
00:29:31,613 --> 00:29:32,739
She didn't do it.

555
00:29:32,906 --> 00:29:34,866
We found the weapon in her car.

556
00:29:34,991 --> 00:29:36,868
Didn't do it.

557
00:29:37,077 --> 00:29:39,913
Unless you have actual evidence
that exonerates her

558
00:29:40,038 --> 00:29:42,207
- we have to charge her.
- If she were the killer

559
00:29:42,332 --> 00:29:44,709
she would have exhibited
some measure of guilt.

560
00:29:44,834 --> 00:29:47,170
All I observed was sincere grief.

561
00:29:50,090 --> 00:29:51,508
Actual evidence.

562
00:29:53,009 --> 00:29:56,012
Okay. The gauntlet's
been thrown down.

563
00:29:58,640 --> 00:30:01,309
When you searched Constance's car,
did you notice any flowers?

564
00:30:01,518 --> 00:30:02,852
No. Why?

565
00:30:03,770 --> 00:30:05,188
She's all yours.

566
00:30:07,982 --> 00:30:09,526
Hey, Osvaldo.

567
00:30:09,901 --> 00:30:11,653
How's it going in the DA's office?

568
00:30:11,820 --> 00:30:14,948
Not so good.
We need to talk about Agent Cho.

569
00:30:15,490 --> 00:30:18,076
Ardiles is prosecuting Rome.

570
00:30:18,993 --> 00:30:21,121
I'm told you visited Rome in jail.
Is that true?

571
00:30:21,246 --> 00:30:22,872
- Why do you wanna know?
- Why...

572
00:30:26,292 --> 00:30:29,462
Uh, because Mr. Rome's lawyer
has sent me an updated witness list

573
00:30:29,587 --> 00:30:31,381
with the name Jayden Stephens on

574
00:30:32,048 --> 00:30:34,134
which is interesting
because as far as I can tell

575
00:30:34,259 --> 00:30:37,679
Jayden Stephens is a convenient figment
of Mr. Rome's imagination.

576
00:30:37,804 --> 00:30:39,389
But now according to Mr. Rome's lawyer

577
00:30:39,514 --> 00:30:41,975
even though you have nothing
to do with this

578
00:30:42,100 --> 00:30:43,935
you said you'd track down
this Mr. Stephens

579
00:30:44,060 --> 00:30:46,062
thereby providing
Mr. Rome with an alibi

580
00:30:46,187 --> 00:30:48,148
potentially screwing my case.

581
00:30:51,192 --> 00:30:52,735
That's why I need to know, Agent Cho.

582
00:30:53,570 --> 00:30:54,779
Answer him.

583
00:30:57,782 --> 00:30:59,409
Yes, I did that.

584
00:31:02,120 --> 00:31:05,790
Agent, do you know who, uh, Asante James
and Rodrick Pierce are?

585
00:31:05,915 --> 00:31:06,958
No.

586
00:31:08,042 --> 00:31:11,087
Well, they're only the, uh, top two
lieutenants in the South Side Mafia.

587
00:31:11,212 --> 00:31:12,589
Probably a dozen bodies on each.

588
00:31:14,048 --> 00:31:15,633
Lawrence Rome worked with them.

589
00:31:16,342 --> 00:31:17,677
You want Lawrence to flip?

590
00:31:18,136 --> 00:31:20,013
- Well, that's the idea.
- Lawrence won't flip.

591
00:31:20,138 --> 00:31:21,764
- Really? Why not?
- He knows they'd kill him.

592
00:31:21,973 --> 00:31:23,516
Right. And you know so much
about that?

593
00:31:23,808 --> 00:31:25,018
More than you, I guess.

594
00:31:26,936 --> 00:31:28,229
Agent, do I have to take this upstairs?

595
00:31:28,354 --> 00:31:30,356
- Because I'm ready.
- No, you don't.

596
00:31:30,482 --> 00:31:31,941
Hey, this is not our case.

597
00:31:32,150 --> 00:31:36,196
Rome's attorney or the DA's office
can look for Jayden Stephens.

598
00:31:36,321 --> 00:31:37,739
We should not get involved.

599
00:31:40,658 --> 00:31:41,743
Good.

600
00:31:43,203 --> 00:31:44,454
Then we're in agreement.

601
00:31:45,705 --> 00:31:47,081
We shouldn't get involved.

602
00:31:47,832 --> 00:31:48,875
Got it.

603
00:32:02,222 --> 00:32:04,766
- Where's the kid?
- Juvenile Services just took him.

604
00:32:06,518 --> 00:32:09,562
- "Let go of me, man. Man, let go of me!"
- "Listen, zip your mouth."

605
00:32:09,687 --> 00:32:11,981
- "Let go of me!"
- Hey! Hold on.

606
00:32:12,607 --> 00:32:13,983
Easy, son, easy.

607
00:32:15,193 --> 00:32:16,528
- What's up?
- I'm Agent Cho.

608
00:32:16,653 --> 00:32:18,321
- I'll take the kid off your hands.
- What?

609
00:32:18,530 --> 00:32:20,657
I made a mistake. Let's just forget
I filed a report, okay?

610
00:32:20,782 --> 00:32:23,743
Too late. Paperwork's been filed.
It's my case now.

611
00:32:24,285 --> 00:32:26,871
Besides, it took me an hour to get here.
I'm not going back empty-handed.

612
00:32:27,664 --> 00:32:28,957
Now do you mind?

613
00:32:30,166 --> 00:32:31,376
Hey, hey.

614
00:32:32,085 --> 00:32:33,836
- Give him to me.
- Sorry. Can't do that.

615
00:32:34,629 --> 00:32:37,340
- He hit you. That's battery.
- Are you kidding me?

616
00:32:37,465 --> 00:32:40,426
- I have to process him now. Paperwork.
- Hold on.

617
00:32:40,552 --> 00:32:41,844
- Bye.
- Hey.

618
00:32:42,011 --> 00:32:43,555
- This is bull!
- What are you doing, man?

619
00:32:43,680 --> 00:32:44,973
Be quiet or I'll give you back.

620
00:33:06,327 --> 00:33:07,870
I thought the police work was over.

621
00:33:08,079 --> 00:33:10,415
Oh, I just stopped by
to congratulate you.

622
00:33:11,082 --> 00:33:12,458
I'm sorry. Me?

623
00:33:13,001 --> 00:33:15,753
You are the new concertmaster,
aren't you?

624
00:33:15,878 --> 00:33:17,547
Now that Constance is in the pokey.

625
00:33:18,006 --> 00:33:19,048
Thanks.

626
00:33:20,592 --> 00:33:23,344
It's not exactly something
that deserves congratulations.

627
00:33:24,262 --> 00:33:25,305
When you heard about the promotion

628
00:33:25,430 --> 00:33:28,016
what was the first thought
that popped into your head?

629
00:33:28,975 --> 00:33:31,978
Sadness... relief.

630
00:33:32,145 --> 00:33:34,022
You know, just last week
I was thinking of leaving here

631
00:33:34,147 --> 00:33:35,523
and trying my luck elsewhere.

632
00:33:37,066 --> 00:33:38,109
Now...

633
00:33:39,068 --> 00:33:40,653
Well, you got what you wanted.

634
00:33:42,322 --> 00:33:45,199
You're pleased and...
yet you feel guilty.

635
00:33:45,366 --> 00:33:47,035
It's perfectly understandable.

636
00:33:48,745 --> 00:33:50,246
I need to get back to rehearsing.

637
00:33:50,955 --> 00:33:52,081
Don't mind me.

638
00:34:08,848 --> 00:34:09,891
Excuse me.

639
00:34:10,892 --> 00:34:12,685
Do you know
if there's a good florist nearby?

640
00:34:20,818 --> 00:34:21,861
What up, Jay?

641
00:34:27,950 --> 00:34:29,160
Jayden Stephens?

642
00:34:30,119 --> 00:34:31,371
Who wants to know?

643
00:34:31,621 --> 00:34:33,331
Hey, CBI. Let me see your hands.

644
00:34:33,831 --> 00:34:35,416
All right.

645
00:34:35,875 --> 00:34:37,418
We're gonna talk
about Lawrence Rome.

646
00:34:37,543 --> 00:34:40,088
We can talk. Let's talk.

647
00:34:51,099 --> 00:34:52,934
Give me your arms!
Give me your arms!

648
00:34:58,356 --> 00:34:59,440
What'd I do?

649
00:35:00,566 --> 00:35:01,609
Get up.

650
00:35:04,112 --> 00:35:05,405
What the hell's going on here?

651
00:35:05,530 --> 00:35:07,031
- Get outta the way.
- Or what?

652
00:35:09,242 --> 00:35:11,369
Keep breathing. You'll be fine.

653
00:35:19,043 --> 00:35:20,086
For you.

654
00:35:22,130 --> 00:35:25,174
- Does it squirt water?
- No. No trick.

655
00:35:26,801 --> 00:35:28,845
Maybe just a little trick.
Catch the killer.

656
00:35:28,970 --> 00:35:30,388
- With a hydrangea?
- Yeah.

657
00:35:30,972 --> 00:35:32,014
How?

658
00:35:32,140 --> 00:35:33,433
Well, wouldn't that be spoiling
the fun?

659
00:35:33,558 --> 00:35:35,518
For you.
Spoiling the fun for you.

660
00:35:35,643 --> 00:35:36,894
That's the fun that matters.

661
00:35:49,905 --> 00:35:52,199
We're dropping charges
against Lawrence Rome.

662
00:35:55,202 --> 00:35:56,245
I see.

663
00:35:56,996 --> 00:35:59,039
Personally, I think the alibi is bogus

664
00:35:59,165 --> 00:36:01,083
but we had to interview
the store owner again.

665
00:36:01,792 --> 00:36:03,753
Now he says, uh,
maybe his ID was wrong.

666
00:36:03,878 --> 00:36:05,296
Maybe it wasn't Lawrence Rome.

667
00:36:06,464 --> 00:36:08,132
Whole thing's gone down the toilet.

668
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:10,968
We had an agreement.

669
00:36:11,093 --> 00:36:13,220
I agreed I shouldn't help.
Didn't say I wouldn't.

670
00:36:13,929 --> 00:36:17,266
From now on, you get nothing
from the DA's office.

671
00:36:17,725 --> 00:36:19,351
No favors, no help...

672
00:36:19,477 --> 00:36:21,562
and not just you, but every
agent in this unit.

673
00:36:22,646 --> 00:36:25,065
You have screwed things
for your people, my friend.

674
00:36:25,649 --> 00:36:27,860
Six months from now, Lawrence Rome
will be back inside

675
00:36:27,985 --> 00:36:31,197
for ripping off another liquor store
his kid'll be back in foster care

676
00:36:31,322 --> 00:36:32,823
and the South Side Mafia

677
00:36:33,032 --> 00:36:34,366
will be stronger than ever.

678
00:36:34,658 --> 00:36:35,826
You're wrong.

679
00:36:37,328 --> 00:36:38,370
You wanna bet on that?

680
00:37:08,359 --> 00:37:10,361
On the stage
either side of the stairs.

681
00:37:24,542 --> 00:37:26,627
Oh, no, no, no, no!

682
00:37:26,752 --> 00:37:28,420
Stop! Stop! Stop!

683
00:37:28,712 --> 00:37:29,797
Kieran!

684
00:37:30,339 --> 00:37:33,425
You're my rock! Never a wrong note.
What is going on?

685
00:37:33,551 --> 00:37:36,428
I'm sorry, maestro, I just...
I'm not feeling very well.

686
00:37:36,554 --> 00:37:37,596
What is the matter?

687
00:37:38,639 --> 00:37:39,765
I can answer that.

688
00:37:41,100 --> 00:37:42,309
What's he doing here?

689
00:37:42,434 --> 00:37:43,936
Fabulous suit, by the way.

690
00:37:44,061 --> 00:37:46,647
Kieran's not so much feeling sick
as he is feeling guilty...

691
00:37:46,772 --> 00:37:49,859
Sick with guilt because
it was him that killed Eleanor.

692
00:37:52,611 --> 00:37:53,696
Come on.

693
00:37:53,904 --> 00:37:55,739
Hydrangeas don't lie.

694
00:37:58,659 --> 00:38:00,744
Well, if they could speak,
they wouldn't lie.

695
00:38:01,036 --> 00:38:02,371
What are you talking about?

696
00:38:02,496 --> 00:38:04,957
Somebody gave Eleanor
a bouquet of hydrangeas

697
00:38:05,082 --> 00:38:06,208
the night of the murder.

698
00:38:09,295 --> 00:38:12,214
"After you shot Eleanor, you swiped them"

699
00:38:13,841 --> 00:38:15,467
"leaving behind a single petal."

700
00:38:17,928 --> 00:38:20,681
And when you saw them, you couldn't
help remembering that night.

701
00:38:20,848 --> 00:38:24,268
You felt guilty.
It killed your concentration.

702
00:38:24,685 --> 00:38:27,813
Come on. Constance killed her.
You found the gun in her car.

703
00:38:27,938 --> 00:38:29,440
Because you framed her.

704
00:38:29,648 --> 00:38:31,567
Precisely.
The question remains...

705
00:38:31,817 --> 00:38:34,862
Why would a man kill
the first chair violinist

706
00:38:35,154 --> 00:38:37,031
and then frame the second chair?

707
00:38:38,073 --> 00:38:40,492
Because with the first and second chair
out of the picture

708
00:38:40,618 --> 00:38:42,119
the third takes first.

709
00:38:42,369 --> 00:38:43,746
Ariel.

710
00:38:43,871 --> 00:38:45,372
Kieran here has a little crush on you.

711
00:38:45,497 --> 00:38:48,250
Well, let's not beat around
the bush here, Kieran.

712
00:38:48,375 --> 00:38:49,877
It's more of an obsession.

713
00:38:50,210 --> 00:38:53,339
He'd heard that you'd been thinking
about leaving the orchestra.

714
00:38:53,464 --> 00:38:56,592
Then he would lose you.
So he had to shake things up.

715
00:38:57,384 --> 00:38:59,136
- Kieran?
- It's not true.

716
00:38:59,261 --> 00:39:01,847
Okay, this is because I played
a few wrong notes? This is crazy!

717
00:39:01,972 --> 00:39:04,808
He told you that you'd eventually
become first chair, didn't he?

718
00:39:04,934 --> 00:39:07,603
It was just a feeling
that he had, a little hunch.

719
00:39:08,270 --> 00:39:10,022
He always had faith in you.

720
00:39:11,357 --> 00:39:13,692
- Ariel. No, Ariel.
- You stay away from me.

721
00:39:13,817 --> 00:39:14,860
Wait, Ariel, wait.
No, no. Wait. Wait.

722
00:39:14,985 --> 00:39:17,446
- Ariel, listen. No, Ariel. Ariel, wait!
- No! Calm down.

723
00:39:17,571 --> 00:39:19,740
- I just wanna make you happy!
- That's enough.

724
00:39:19,865 --> 00:39:22,034
- Maestro, take five.
- Okay.

725
00:39:22,201 --> 00:39:23,243
Break, everyone.

726
00:39:24,078 --> 00:39:26,330
Eleanor was nothing compared
to Ariel.

727
00:39:26,455 --> 00:39:27,998
She didn't have the technique.

728
00:39:29,083 --> 00:39:32,795
So after rehearsal that night, I followed
Eleanor to her performance.

729
00:39:52,773 --> 00:39:54,316
Why'd you take the flowers?

730
00:39:55,067 --> 00:39:58,070
He didn't think Eleanor deserved them.
Isn't that right?

731
00:39:58,237 --> 00:40:02,658
Ariel is ten times the player.
She deserved the recognition.

732
00:40:04,660 --> 00:40:06,245
If I had to give it to her

733
00:40:07,413 --> 00:40:08,622
so be it.

734
00:40:09,581 --> 00:40:10,791
Very gallant.

735
00:40:11,291 --> 00:40:14,044
Still, I wouldn't expect a conjugal.

736
00:40:19,049 --> 00:40:20,259
Dad!

737
00:40:24,096 --> 00:40:25,806
Oh, what's up, man?

738
00:40:27,683 --> 00:40:29,852
- I missed you so much.
- Oh!

739
00:40:30,144 --> 00:40:32,855
Look at you.
God, look at you.

740
00:40:33,313 --> 00:40:34,356
Come on.

741
00:40:35,858 --> 00:40:37,067
I missed you.

742
00:40:39,236 --> 00:40:40,279
Lawrence.

743
00:40:42,740 --> 00:40:44,324
All right. Give me a minute.

744
00:40:45,284 --> 00:40:46,326
Okay.

745
00:40:49,872 --> 00:40:51,123
I talked to the Gang Unit.

746
00:40:51,248 --> 00:40:53,083
If you haven't jumped out in a month
they'll let me know.

747
00:40:53,625 --> 00:40:54,918
I said I would.

748
00:40:57,546 --> 00:40:59,131
You have a chance, don't mess it up.

749
00:41:00,382 --> 00:41:02,092
What's this punk saying to you, Dad?

750
00:41:02,301 --> 00:41:04,845
Easy. Easy, little man.
We just, we just talking.

751
00:41:05,345 --> 00:41:07,681
Hey, Cho. We got a new one.
Heading out in a minute.

752
00:41:10,017 --> 00:41:11,268
Thanks, Mr. Rigsby.

753
00:41:11,727 --> 00:41:15,064
- I really appreciate everything.
- Uh, yeah. Um, no problem.

754
00:41:21,278 --> 00:41:23,947
That was weird.
